  "query_preview": "..\n\nAn upper ridge axis established over northwest Montana is preceded\nby weak shortwaves in the flow and increasing southeast winds at\nthe surface. Observations at South Sawmill and a few others in and\naround Fort Peck Lake have shown sustained wind speeds increasing\nalready tonight. Given trends, have nudged the short term wind\nforecast toward the gustier hires solutions in support of\nmaintaining the Lake Wind Advisory for Fort Peck Lake through noon\nMonday. After that time, breezy conditions should shift toward the\neast along the MT/ND border as the ridge axis advances closer to\nthe CWA. Meanwhile, this ridge will help support seasonably mild\nand dry weather conditions for NE Montana through the middle of\nthe week.\n\nOn Thursday, a deep western U.S. trough will translate eastward\nwith a shortwave lobe pinwheeling northeastward across southeast\nMontana out ahead of it Thursday night and Friday. This will lend\ndynamic support in conjunction with Pacific moisture to increase\nprecipitation chances for the area Thursday night into the\nFriday along with markedly cooler temperatures. Thermal profiles \nhowever should remain warm enough to support rain, though a little\nsnow may mix in near the Canadian border or higher elevations of \nthe Little Rockies by Friday night as the precipitation ends.\nCurrent NBM mean shows an early-bird look at a range of a quarter\nto a half of an inch of storm total QPF with lesser amounts toward\nWibaux.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nNBM was largely used in support of the going forecast cycle.\nHowever, hires model solutions were used as a nudge to near term\nwinds in support of the Lake Wind Advisory for Fort Peck Lake for\nMonday. Looking at solid ensemble consensus on ridging bringing\nabout warm and dry conditions for the midweek with the general\nidea toward cooler and wetter weather late in the week. The timing\nand details of precipitation placement and amount are still to be\nrefined however given that it is at later time scales.",
